                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Everyone compares Hero-U to the Quest for Glory series, and there's good reason for that. It's an adventure/RPG hybrid with plenty of charm, interesting characters to meet, and tedious tasks to work your way through.\n\nI enjoyed Hero-U, but with caveats. The game is overly long. There is busywork littered throughout, intentionally so, as you progress your skills. The gameplay, such as it is, could optimistically be described as \"sufficient.\"\n\nBut the aforementioned charm really is here in spades. There's a wit and optimism to Hero-U, just as there was to the Quest for Glory games, that's difficult to describe and even harder to find in other titles.\n\nI'd heartily recommend Hero-U to anyone who enjoyed Quest for Glory. For those who never played those older games, I'd probably recommend booting them up first. Retro they may be, but Hero-U isn't much more evolved, and if that older series can't keep your attention then this tribute to it certainly won't do any better.",
